.\" uwebserver(1) -- the manual page of uwebserver, Exponential Velocity.
.\" Kept equal to `uwebserver --help` by tests/unit-uwebserver-docs.php.
.TH UWEBSERVER 1 "2026-09-30" "Exponential Velocity 0.0.4.42" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uwebserver \- a small web server: static files or built-in answers, over HTTP/1.1 and HTTPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwebserver
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B uwebserver
\fB\-\-root\fR=\fIDIR\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B uwebserver
\fB\-\-config\fR=\fIFILE\fR \fB\-\-check\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uwebserver
answers HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/1.0, over TCP and over TLS, from one event loop per
process. With
.BR \-\-root ,
it serves the files under a directory: GET and HEAD, conditional requests, one
byte range, precompressed
.I .gz
files and, when asked for, directory listings. Without it, it answers
.IR / ,
.I /json
and
.I /health
itself, as a baseline for benchmarks of Exponential Velocity.
.PP
It listens on
.B 127.0.0.1:8000
unless told otherwise, and never on every interface unless that is asked for.
As root it serves only with
.B \-\-user
(to which it changes once the ports are open) or
.BR \-\-allow\-root .
.PP
Every long option also works with one dash
.RB ( \-root=DIR ),
a value may follow as
.BI \-\- name = value
or as the next word, one\-letter options bundle
.RB ( \-qd ),
and
.B \-\-
ends the options. Every switch has a
.BI \-\-no\- name
form. Long names are never abbreviated. A
.I SIZE
may end in k, m or g (powers of 1024); a number of
.I SECONDS
of 0 means no limit.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit. \fB\-v\fR, \fB\-version\fR, \fB\-\-copyright\fR and \fB\-copyright\fR do the same.
.TP
.B \-\-about
Print the version with the build details and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Read settings from \fIFILE\fR (see \fBCONFIGURATION FILE\fR).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-check ", " \-\-test\-config
Check the configuration and everything the start needs (the root, the
certificate and key, the logs, the user), print the addresses it would serve
on, serve nothing, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print every setting in effect, in the configuration file format, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Log errors only.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log connection events too: timeouts, malformed requests, refused connections.
.SS Listening
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen =[\fIADDR\fR:]\fIPORT\fR
Serve HTTP on \fIADDR\fR:\fIPORT\fR. Repeatable. \fIADDR\fR is a numeric IPv4
address, an IPv6 address in brackets (\fB[::1]\fR; an IPv6 listener takes IPv6
only), \fB*\fR for every IPv4 address, or \fBlocalhost\fR; without it, the
\fB\-\-bind\fR address.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
The address of \fB\-\-port\fR and \fB\-\-tls\-port\fR (127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Serve HTTP on the \fB\-\-bind\fR address at \fIPORT\fR (8000). The HTTP
listener of \fB\-\-bind\fR:\fB\-\-port\fR is there when either is given, or
when no \fB\-\-listen\fR and no \fB\-\-tls\-listen\fR are.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-listen =[\fIADDR\fR:]\fIPORT\fR
Serve HTTPS there. Repeatable. Needs \fB\-\-cert\fR and \fB\-\-key\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Serve HTTPS on the \fB\-\-bind\fR address at \fIPORT\fR (8443, which is used
when \fB\-\-cert\fR is given without a \fB\-\-tls\-listen\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-reuse\-port
Let other servers share the ports (SO_REUSEPORT). Off: a port in use is an
error, never shared.
.TP
.BR \-\-backlog =\fIN\fR
Connections waiting to be accepted (511).
.SS Content
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root =\fIDIR\fR
Serve the files under \fIDIR\fR. Nothing outside it is ever reached: files are
opened beneath it (openat2, RESOLVE_BENEATH), a path with a \fB..\fR segment,
an encoded \fB/\fR or NUL is refused, and so is a link that leads out.
Without \fB\-\-root\fR, the built-in answers.
.TP
.BR \-\-index =\fINAMES\fR
The files that answer for a directory, separated by commas (index.html).
.TP
.B \-\-directory\-listing
List a directory that has no index file (off: 403).
.TP
.B \-\-hidden\-files
Serve names that start with a dot (off: they answer 404, so \fI.git\fR or
\fI.env\fR are never served by mistake).
.TP
.BR \-\-symlinks =\fBinside\fR|\fBnever\fR
Follow symbolic links that stay inside \fIDIR\fR (inside; a link with an
absolute target is resolved from / and so never is), or none at all.
.TP
.BR \-\-mime\-types =\fIFILE\fR
More media types, in the \fImime.types\fR format; they win over the built-in
table.
.TP
.BR \-\-default\-type =\fITYPE\fR
The type of a file whose extension is not known (application/octet-stream).
.TP
.BR \-\-charset =\fINAME\fR
Added to text types (utf-8). Empty: none.
.TP
.BR \-\-cache\-control =\fIVALUE\fR
The Cache-Control header of files (none).
.TP
.B \-\-etag
Send ETag and answer If-None-Match and If-Range with it (on).
.TP
.B \-\-gzip\-static
Send \fIFILE\fR.gz, with Content-Encoding: gzip, to a client that accepts gzip
(off).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-header =\(aq\fINAME\fR: \fIVALUE\fR\(aq
Add a header to every response. Repeatable. Headers the server sets itself
(Content-Length, Connection, Date ...) cannot be given.
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-name =\fINAME\fR
The value of the Server header (uwebserver; no version is ever sent).
.TP
.B \-\-server\-header
Send a Server header (on).
.SS Limits and timeouts
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workers =\fIN\fR
Worker processes (1, at most 256). A worker that ends is replaced; workers
that keep ending stop the server.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-connections =\fIN\fR
Open connections per worker (1024). More are closed at once.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-requests =\fIN\fR
Requests per connection (1000); 0: no limit.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-header\-size =\fISIZE\fR
The request line and headers together (8k; 1k to 1m). Larger: 431.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-uri\-length =\fISIZE\fR
The request target (4k). Longer: 414.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-body\-size =\fISIZE\fR
A request body, which is read and discarded (1m). Larger: 413.
.TP
.BR \-\-header\-timeout =\fISECONDS\fR
To receive a whole request head, from its first byte (10).
.TP
.BR \-\-read\-timeout =\fISECONDS\fR
Between reads of a request body (30).
.TP
.BR \-\-write\-timeout =\fISECONDS\fR
Without progress sending a response (30).
.TP
.BR \-\-keepalive\-timeout =\fISECONDS\fR
Idle between two requests of a connection (5); 0: no keep-alive.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-handshake\-timeout =\fISECONDS\fR
To complete a TLS handshake (10).
.SS TLS
.TP
.BR \-\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
The certificate, PEM; it may hold the chain after it.
.TP
.BR \-\-key =\fIFILE\fR
Its private key, PEM. Refused when other users may read or change it, or its
group may change it; a warning when its group may read it.
.TP
.BR \-\-chain =\fIFILE\fR
More chain certificates, PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-min\-version =\fB1.2\fR|\fB1.3\fR
The oldest TLS version accepted (1.2).
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-ciphers =\fILIST\fR
TLS 1.2 ciphers, an OpenSSL cipher list (default: ECDHE key exchange with
AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 only).
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-ciphersuites =\fILIST\fR
TLS 1.3 suites (OpenSSL's default).
.SS Logging
.TP
.BR \-\-access\-log =\fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR|\fBoff\fR
Log each request to \fIFILE\fR, or to standard output with \fB\-\fR (off).
Bytes a client sent are escaped (\ex\fIHH\fR in text, \eu00\fIHH\fR in JSON),
so a request can never add a line or a field.
.TP
.BR \-\-access\-log\-format =\fIFORMAT\fR
\fBcommon\fR, \fBcombined\fR or \fBjson\fR (combined).
.TP
.BR \-\-error\-log =\fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR
Log messages to \fIFILE\fR, or to standard error with \fB\-\fR (\-).
Files are created with mode 0640 and never through a symbolic link.
.SS Process
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run in the background. The command returns once the server serves, with 0, or
with 1 when it could not start.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground (the default).
.TP
.BR \-\-pid\-file =\fIFILE\fR
Write the process id to \fIFILE\fR and hold a lock on it while running; a
second server with the same file does not start.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user =\fIUSER\fR
Run as \fIUSER\fR (a name or a number, not root) once the ports are open and
the certificate, key and logs are opened. Needs root.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group =\fIGROUP\fR
Run as \fIGROUP\fR (default: the group of \fIUSER\fR). Supplementary groups
are dropped.
.TP
.BR \-\-chroot =\fIDIR\fR
Change the root directory to \fIDIR\fR before dropping to \fIUSER\fR. Needs
root. \fB\-\-root\fR is opened before, so it may lie inside \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-root
Serve as root without \fB\-\-user\fR. Refused otherwise.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
One setting per line: the long name of an option without its dashes, then its
value, as \fIname\fR = \fIvalue\fR or \fIname value\fR; a switch alone, as
\fIname\fR = yes|no, or as \fBno\-\fR\fIname\fR. A line whose first non-blank
character is \fB#\fR is a comment. A value may be quoted to keep blanks at its
ends. Repeatable settings (\fBlisten\fR, \fBtls\-listen\fR, \fBheader\fR) are
given once per value.
.PP
The file is read first, then the command line; a repeatable option given on
the command line replaces the file's values. \fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR,
\fB\-\-config\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR and \fB\-\-print\-config\fR are not settings.
An unknown setting or a bad value stops the program with the file and line.
\fB\-\-print\-config\fR prints a file that reads back to the same settings.
.PP
.nf
    # /etc/uwebserver.conf
    root = /srv/www
    listen = 127.0.0.1:8000
    listen = [::1]:8000
    user = www
    access\-log = /var/log/uwebserver/access.log
    gzip\-static
    header = X\-Frame\-Options: DENY
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UWEBSERVER_CONFIG
The configuration file, when \fB\-\-config\fR is not given. No other variable
changes what the server does: an inherited environment must not change what
it exposes.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT ", " SIGHUP
Stop: close the ports, close idle connections, let those in the middle of a
request finish (for at most 10 seconds), then exit 0. With \fB\-\-workers\fR,
the parent stops the workers the same way.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; with \fB\-\-check\fR, the configuration is valid.
.TP
.B 1
The server could not start (a port in use, a file it cannot open, a key that
does not match, root without \fB\-\-user\fR), stopped on an error, or
\fB\-\-check\fR found a problem.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown option, a missing or bad value, options that
contradict each other, or a bad configuration file. Nothing was started.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B uwebserver \-\-root=/srv/www
The files of /srv/www on http://127.0.0.1:8000/.
.TP
.B uwebserver \-r /srv/www \-l \(aq*:80\(aq \-u www \-\-access\-log=/var/log/uweb.log
Every IPv4 address, port 80, as the user www, with an access log.
.TP
.B uwebserver \-r . \-\-tls\-listen=8443 \-\-cert=site.crt \-\-key=site.key \-\-tls\-min\-version=1.3
HTTPS with TLS 1.3 only on 127.0.0.1:8443, beside HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8000.
.TP
.B uwebserver \-\-port=8081 \-\-workers=4
The built-in answers, for a benchmark, from four processes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/uwebserver.md
The full documentation, in the Exponential Velocity tree.
